@id n2_choira
# DRAFT
# Brother Wulfric on the south walk at dusk (night 2), rubbing his knees. Background; crabbed.
# The drowned merchant, or the abbot's extra hour of prayer; the abbot has dreamed badly since Michaelmas.
== start
(Old Brother Wulfric on the south walk, rubbing his knees.)
-> dead [if died_merchant]
-> plain

== dead
Wulfric {amused}: A drunk drowns in our fishpond, and the abbot goes about with a face like he's seen the Devil.
Wulfric {weary}: In my day a drunk who drowned was a drunk who drowned.
-> topics

== plain
Wulfric {weary}: The abbot had us on our knees an hour after chapter, praying for the house. My knees are older than his.
-> topics

== again
Wulfric {amused}: Still here, boy? Go and ring something.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n2_choira_abbot] What is the abbot afraid of, brother? -> abbot

== abbot [set n2_choira_abbot]
Wulfric {grave}: Bad dreams. He's had them since Michaelmas. At his age you dream of the grave, and he's earned it.
-> end

== leave
Wulfric {weary}: On the mark tonight, boy.
